  "body": "Follow-up from the review of PR #3082 (#2965), comment 7051611241. The decision file `docs/decisions/2965-first-traverse-rotary.md` records both limits.\n\n1. A machine with two rotary axes: the swept law of #2965 turns the work about one fitted axis only. The traverse before the rotary words can meet work that the second rotary has also turned.\n2. A multi-axis kind on a machine whose table tilts: the #2901 tip law reads the part frame. When the table tilts the work, the part frame at the first traverse is the pose that the previous program left, not the pose of the operation.\n\nRisk: the first rapid can go through the stock, the part or the fixture, and no law refuses it.\n\nWork:\n1. For each case, read the work through every pose that the previous program can leave (the full range of each rotary that turns the work), or refuse the operation by name.\n2. Add pinning tests for each case.\n",
